2024-02-23T20:48:20 |Date: Fri, 14 Jun 2019 14:27:29 +0000
2024-02-23T20:48:20 |Subject: [PATCH] Delete totally bogus code specifically targetted at mandoc
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | which tried to figure out whether mandoc supported UTF-8 output (which it has
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | been doing since 2011) and which passed the -T locale option (which has been
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | the default since 2014 and always will) but which required the -V option to
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | work (which was deleted half a decade ago and will not come back). Nowadays,
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | it is safe to assume that mandoc just works with UTF-8 on both the input and
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | output sides - in literally each and every operating system providing a
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | mandoc port or package, even those that are seriously lagging behind. This
2024-02-23T20:48:20 | patch will also be pushed upstream. OK tb@
2024-02-23T20:48:20 |
