2024-02-23T20:48:47 |Subject: [PATCH] Fix Perl tests in OpenBSD regress.
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |Disable Perl test t/porting/exec-bit.t as it only checks permissions.
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |The x-bit in OpenBSD CVS tree does not match Perl distribution tar.
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |This is known and accepted.
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |Set permission of Test-Harness source.sh and source_args.sh to
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |executable as Perl uses it to test module features. Stay close to
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |upstream. During regress, set the x-bit of the files in obj
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |directory. Do not touch src tree, it might be read-only.
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |
2024-02-23T20:48:47 |discussed with anton@; OK afresh1@
